course: dictionary
lesson: 2470
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer chose. «The dashboard is the car talking to the driver.» The words car and driver tell you that dashboard means the panel in front of the driver.
explain: Read the words around the word. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about a car, use the car meaning. If it is about a computer or an app, use the screen meaning. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look for small clue words too. «A warning light on the dashboard» tells you that the dashboard is in a car, because car warning lights are on the panel in front of the driver. When the clues are not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A dashboard is the panel at the front of a car, under the windscreen, with the speedometer, dials, lights and controls.
fact: On a computer or app, a dashboard is a screen that shows the most important information at a glance, often with charts and numbers.
fact: Long ago, a dashboard on a horse-drawn carriage was a board at the front to stop mud splashing the driver.
fact: «Dashboard warning lights all come on briefly when the car starts», to show the bulbs work, and then they go off unless something is wrong.
fact: The same word can have different meanings in different subjects, so the context tells you which one to use.
exercise: «The dashboard lights came on when Dad started the car.» What is the dashboard in this sentence? | *The panel at the front of the car with dials and lights | A wooden table in the kitchen | A board to stop mud splashing the driver | A screen of charts and numbers
exercise: A computer screen shows the day's scores in charts and numbers, so the most important information is seen at a glance. What is this screen called? | A windscreen | A carriage | A bonnet | *A dashboard
exercise: In the phrase «a warning light on the dashboard», which word is the clue that dashboard means the car panel? | Screen | *Warning light | Charts | Dashboard
test: «On the dashboard, the speedometer showed forty miles an hour.» What does dashboard mean here? | A table for dinner | *The panel in a car | A board at the front of a carriage | A computer screen of charts
test: A teacher says, «Look at the dashboard to see today's visits to our class website.» What does dashboard mean here? | A board at the front of a carriage | A panel under a windscreen | A kind of car engine | *A screen showing key information at a glance
exam: Which meaning of dashboard is used in «The dashboard is the car talking to the driver», and what clue shows it? | The computer screen, because talking shows it is online | Any meaning will do, because the sentence is unclear | *The car panel, because car and driver are clue words | The carriage board, because talking shows it is old
